      "message": "I feel like I\u0027m missing something important as to why that\u0027s needed for us, as that would likely mean any embedded library never worked till now?\n\nAs can be seen here https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/jni/com_android_internal_content_NativeLibraryHelper.cpp;l\u003d197 any app with extractNativeLibs set to false requires native libraries in zips to be stored, not deflated.\n\nOur setup is as following:\nlib_with_jni.aar is an AAR with only a JNI library in it, libjni.so\n\nandroid_library_import {\n    name: \"lib_with_jni-nodeps\",\n    aars: [\"lib_with_jni.aar\"],\n    extract_jni: true,\n}\n\nandroid_library {\n   name: \"lib_with_jni-lib\",\n   sdk_version: \"current\",\n   min_sdk_version: \"33\",\n   static_libs: [\"lib_with_jni-nodeps\"],\n}\n\nandroid_app {\n    name: \"app_with_jni\",\n    \u003csnip\u003e\n    static_libs: [\"lib_with_jni-lib\"],\n    use_embedded_native_libs: true,\n}\n\nThe final APK has lib/$ARCH/libjni.so zipped as defN ( deflate ) and can\u0027t be installed via adb install and/or included in system images ( as the lib won\u0027t be extracted per manifest entry )",
